+# Phase 12 — Account lifecycle and production identity linkage
+
+Release target: **EduPath BD v0.9.4 / Android+iOS build 22**
+
+## Objective
+
+Close a production account-lifecycle gap: a user who can create an account must be able to remove the application account and its linked sign-in identity without relying on mutable email matching.
+
+## Implemented
+
+### Stable Firebase identity linkage
+
+- `User.firebaseUid` is a nullable unique field so existing databases can migrate safely.
+- Registration stores the Firebase UID immediately.
+- Session synchronization matches by Firebase UID or email and backfills/updates the UID for existing users.
+- The new migration adds the field and unique index without forcing a destructive backfill.
+
+### Self-service student account deletion
+
+- `DELETE /api/me/account` is authenticated, STUDENT-role scoped and rate limited.
+- The request must contain the signed-in username as an explicit typed confirmation.
+- In production the API deletes the linked Firebase identity and then deletes the Prisma user; user-owned relational data cascades through the existing foreign-key model.
+- Demo mode deletes the disposable demo student's profile, shortlist, applications, interactions, reports, comments, votes and ratings so the flow remains testable without real credentials.
+- Admin/moderator accounts are not exposed to this self-service route because admin audit retention and operator handoff require a separate controlled workflow.
+
+### Device cleanup after deletion
+
+After a successful account deletion the client:
+
+- signs out any remaining Firebase client session;
+- clears the persisted pathway profile and app session;
+- clears comparison/scholarship selections and public API cache;
+- cancels stored browser timers and native deadline notifications;
+- returns the application to a clean signed-out state.
+
+### QA evidence
+
+- API verification covers wrong-confirmation rejection and successful disposable demo-account deletion.
+- Release verification checks the migration, Firebase UID persistence, deletion route, confirmation UI and local reminder cleanup.
+- The existing Account & privacy browser smoke path continues to exercise the entry point on responsive layouts.
+
+## Production boundary
+
+The source is production-oriented, but v1.0 still requires the real Firebase Admin project, PostgreSQL deployment, Supabase Storage, HTTPS API, signed AAB and physical-phone/hosted-CI proof. Account deletion should be re-tested against the real Firebase project before store submission.
